sec.p:
To assess the effects of sacubitril/valsartan on metabolic indices, we pooled the differences between pre- and post-treatment values and reported the findings as the pooled mean difference (MD) with 95% confidence interval (CI). As such, for the included RCTs, MDs for the metabolic indices were obtained only from the intervention group or from those receiving sacubitril/valsartan. The standard error of the mean change in the outcomes was calculated from published baseline and follow-up means and standard deviations (SDs) using the formula for paired data:\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$\mathrm{SE}(\mathrm{change})\;=\sqrt{}{\left[\mathrm{SD}{(\mathrm{baseline})}^2\;+\;\mathrm{SD}{(\mathrm{follow}-\mathrm{up})}^2\;-\;2\;\times\;\mathrm r\;\times\;\mathrm{SD}(\mathrm{baseline})\;\times\;\mathrm{SD}(\mathrm{follow}-\mathrm{up})\right]}\;/\;\sqrt{}{\mathrm n}$$\end{document}
